# The app moved from GitHub Pages to plain FTPS hosting (see
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml), so GitHub Pages' automatic "serve 404.html
# for any unknown path" behavior no longer applies - without it, a direct
# link/reload on e.g. /memory/game hits the web server's own 404 page instead
# of this single-page app. This restores the same behavior on Apache: any
# unmatched request under /memory/ gets 404.html, whose existing
# redirect-with-encoded-path script (see public/404.html, index.html) then
# hands control back to the app's router.
ErrorDocument 404 /memory/404.html
